{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1322256-what-predates-the-mythic-age-in-mage-s-history","id":1322256,"title":"What predates the Mythic Age in Mage's history?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-04T11:24:53-07:00","id":1322256,"title":"What predates the Mythic Age in Mage's history?","content":"So the Wiki says the Mythic Age is between the fall of Rome and the end of the Middle Ages. A time when monsters and dragons and stuff roamed, before the Order of Reason, when the Gauntlet was weaker.<br /> <br /> So what came before it? How was Mage, Magic, spirits, the Umbra, etc, different in the classical era and Bronze Age?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T14:44:05-07:00","id":1322285,"title":"","content":"Dead Magic 1 suggested that the era of the Roman Empire was in many ways similar to the present. It's extremely vague about it, but the implication is that the present Technocracy-Tradition conflict is an echo of previous conflicts.<br /> <br /> That being said, I don't think the setting otherwise mentions this idea. Though it's worth mentioning that much of the history of the setting is told in-character and is often very mythological.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T05:47:36-07:00","id":1322394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1322256-what-predates-the-mythic-age-in-mage-s-history?p=1322285#post1322285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's extremely vague about it, but the implication is that the present Technocracy-Tradition conflict is an echo of previous conflicts.<br /> <br /> That being said, I don't think the setting otherwise mentions this idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never tought about that, but I think there may be other instances where we can find this &quot;eternal return&quot; thing<br /> <br /> For instance, it's states that the Spheres were invented in the Grand Convocation, but in ages past the Pharaoh Thotmes III made a convocation of mages, and these codified &quot;The Nine Cornerstones of Reality&quot;.<br /> <br /> And this egyptian court was divided betwen two groups: The Cupbearers of Aset (antecesors of the Council of Nine) and the Reed of Djehuty (antecesors of the Technocracy). It's said that this period of time brought wonders, but the conflicts between these groups ended this golden era of magick<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T09:26:29-07:00","id":1322434,"title":"","content":"Which book is that in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T10:14:40-07:00","id":1322447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1322256-what-predates-the-mythic-age-in-mage-s-history?p=1322434#post1322434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which book is that in?</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 has a sidebar on them (pg.122). Order of Hermes Revised mentions them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T10:13:01-07:00","id":1322618,"title":"","content":"What we call the mythic ages is basically the &quot;high&quot; mythic age. So you could say that before that, it was the middle mythic age","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T13:23:29-07:00","id":1391767,"title":"","content":"I think exalted was originally supposed to be the prehistory for the world of darkness","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14453-tamuz","name":"Tamuz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T14:02:54-07:00","id":1391774,"title":"","content":"It was, but that's a long, long time before Rome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T20:44:09-07:00","id":1391849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1322256-what-predates-the-mythic-age-in-mage-s-history?p=1322618#post1322618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What we call the mythic ages is basically the &quot;high&quot; mythic age. So you could say that before that, it was the middle mythic age</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but note that the 'High' Mythic Age is a conceit of later mages, many from Traditions or sects who see this as a time of unchallenged authority (i.e., they assume that they were in the ascendancy and those sects or views that would later give rise to the Order of Reason and then the Technocracy were marginalized). It's also a specifically Eurocentric take on magickal history. A more nuanced look at what we can say about the history and archaeology of that time might not support the conceit as completely as its advocates want.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;</span>Explanations exist; they have existed for all time; there is always a well-known solution to every human problem \u2014 neat, plausible, and wrong.<span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;<br /> - H.L. Mencken</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/467-bob-the-skull","name":"Bob the Skull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T21:01:05-07:00","id":1391854,"title":"","content":"&quot;Know, O prince, that between the years that the oceans drank Atlantis and the gleaming cities, and the rise of the sons of Aryas, there was an age undreamed of, when shining kingdoms lay spread across the world like blue mantels beneath the stars...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25651,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","user":"Marko Markoko","date":". 05-29-2020, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T22:19:17-07:00","id":1391863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1322256-what-predates-the-mythic-age-in-mage-s-history?p=1322434#post1322434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which book is that in?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage: The Sorcerers' Crusade's core book, which actually has a really in depth multi-page timeline covering the history of the Awakened up until around the 16th century AD, including a bunch of details about stuff from ancient Egypt, parts of Africa and Asia, and various obscure factions throughout history.<br /> <br /> My own theories are that anything before around 2000 - 3000 BC is probably not exactly Reality as we know it, and that what archeological and other evidence of these prehistoric periods that exist in the WoD are probably remnants of a multifaceted reality full of blood gods, dragon kings, fey lords, angels, demons, and who knows what else.<br /> After this antediluvian age collapsed into a single reality, you probably have a long period in which history and myth are close to the same thing. In the West, especially around the Mediterranean region, this probably ended in the Bronze Age with what we remember as the Trojan War and the Bronze Age Collapse. In India, you have the end of the Vedic period, and in China, the Spring &amp; Autumn period.<br /> I think the Mythic Age really goes back as far to Classical Greece and Late Period Egypt, as well as Sixteen Kingdoms/Mahajanapadas era India, Warring States era China, and Persia's Achaemenid Empire. This period is constantly interspersed with various empires (Alexander the Great, the Romans, the Qin dynasty, etc.) trying to assert a certain degree of cultural dominance, and a recurring theme of factions within those empires often clashing over influence of the culture as a whole. Rome had its Cults of Mercury, the Brotherhood of the Rule, and rival Celestial Chorus forerunners, while China has its Legalists, assorted Akashic factions, and so forth. I tend to place the 13th and 14th centuries, especially the Black Death and the Mongol invasions, as the end of the Mythic Age in Eurasia.<br /> Such are my thoughts, at least.<br /> <br /> I think a clearer division would be something like:<ul><li>The Unknown/Antediluvian - before @2500 BC</li> <li>The High Mythic Age - @2000 BC - @400 BC</li> <li>The Mystic Age - @300 BC - @1350 AD</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 05-27-2020, 01:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T06:09:45-07:00","id":1391907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bob the Skull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1322256-what-predates-the-mythic-age-in-mage-s-history?p=1391849#post1391849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but note that the 'High' Mythic Age is a conceit of later mages, many from Traditions or sects who see this as a time of unchallenged authority (i.e., they assume that they were in the ascendancy and those sects or views that would later give rise to the Order of Reason and then the Technocracy were marginalized). </div> </div> </div> </div>Ironic, considering that the antecedents of the Traditions were actually the marginal ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T06:46:49-07:00","id":1391913,"title":"","content":"I know that that's what MRev likes to claim; but is it really true? At the very least, I have trouble buying the notion that the Order of Hermes was actually among \u201cthe marginal ones\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T07:05:16-07:00","id":1391919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1322256-what-predates-the-mythic-age-in-mage-s-history?p=1391913#post1391913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that that's what MRev likes to claim; but is it really true? At the very least, I have trouble buying the notion that the Order of Hermes was actually among \u201cthe marginal ones\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>If all of your time is spent cloistered at the edge of society doing experiments, you're closer to that than you are to being a ruler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T07:20:48-07:00","id":1391923,"title":"","content":"But it's not a binary distinction. And frankly, for all their bluster, the Technocrats aren't really rulers either. They like to <i>think</i> of themselves that way; but in practice, most of them\u2026 <br /> <br /> \u2026spend most of their time cloistered at the edge of society doing experiments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T11:30:28-07:00","id":1392005,"title":"","content":"Besides, I'm not totally convinced that Paradox hasn't retroactively rewritten history to conform more closely to the modern-day Consensus...in which case all bets are truly off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;</span>Explanations exist; they have existed for all time; there is always a well-known solution to every human problem \u2014 neat, plausible, and wrong.<span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;<br /> - H.L. Mencken</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/467-bob-the-skull","name":"Bob the Skull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T12:04:15-07:00","id":1392013,"title":"","content":"Have I commented on the irony of the World of Darkness IP (including Mage) being owned by a company named \u201cParadox\u201d?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T12:26:12-07:00","id":1392020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1322256-what-predates-the-mythic-age-in-mage-s-history?p=1391863#post1391863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mage: The Sorcerers' Crusade's core book, which actually has a really in depth multi-page timeline covering the history of the Awakened up until around the 16th century AD, including a bunch of details about stuff from ancient Egypt, parts of Africa and Asia, and various obscure factions throughout history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately I don't have that book, but thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T12:33:04-07:00","id":1392024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1322256-what-predates-the-mythic-age-in-mage-s-history#post1322256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what came before it? </div> </div> </div> </div>Stone age Mage! And then the Hyborean age with Conan and Thulsa Doom! <br /> <br /> Edit: Then the rise of classical civilization...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T15:39:58-07:00","id":1392069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1322256-what-predates-the-mythic-age-in-mage-s-history?p=1392013#post1392013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have I commented on the irony of the World of Darkness IP (including Mage) being owned by a company named \u201cParadox\u201d?</div> </div> </div> </div>Be careful commenting on things like that. Wrinkle moonlights in Entropy Effects connected to intellectual property law.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;</span>Explanations exist; they have existed for all time; there is always a well-known solution to every human problem \u2014 neat, plausible, and wrong.<span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;<br /> - H.L. Mencken</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/467-bob-the-skull","name":"Bob the Skull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T16:48:31-07:00","id":1392075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1322256-what-predates-the-mythic-age-in-mage-s-history?p=1392020#post1392020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately I don't have that book, but thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can get the <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/201/Mage-The-Sorcerers-Crusade\" target=\"_blank\">pdf version</a> from drivethrurpg. (I'm a little disappointed that they don't have a bundle for it, as a number of the sourcebooks are also pretty good.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1322256-what-predates-the-mythic-age-in-mage-s-history?p=1392024#post1392024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stone age Mage! And then the Hyborean age with Conan and Thulsa Doom!</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to imagine the antediluvian world as being this multifaceted thing of overlapping realities, including but not limited to First City of Caine and his brood, the Mokole's Age of Dragon Kings, Stone Age Impergium, the land that knew neither Death nor Oblivion, the Overseers of the Tapestry, Changeling's Time of Legends, the Middle Kingdom's Age of Legends, and so forth. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T18:40:28-07:00","id":1392089,"title":"","content":"I will also mention my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1381358-ages-of-darkness?p=1381985#post1381985\">Savage Sands</a> setting concept from my Ages of Darkness thread, about the ancient (like 4th millennium BC) war between Horus and Set that gave birth to the Egyptian mummies. Generally a Werewolf/Mummy/Mage crossover with certain Vampire elements, this would predate the Cupbearers and the Reed. I think there's an interesting idea to be explored here with a number of mage fellowships devoted to specific gods that have clear parallels or associations with more modern factions. Thoth with the Hermetics, Ptah with the Craftmasons and/or Etherites, Ra with Celestial Chorus, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T06:26:54-07:00","id":1392178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1322256-what-predates-the-mythic-age-in-mage-s-history?p=1392075#post1392075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like to imagine the antediluvian world as being this multifaceted thing of overlapping realities</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds more likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T07:48:13-07:00","id":1392191,"title":"","content":"It's the notion that was put forward in <b>Demon: the Fallen</b>; and <b>Ascension</b> revisited the notion with its Fractured Cosmology: according to that part of the finale of the Revised line, even the modern World of Darkness is a multifaceted thing with overlapping realities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T12:24:41-07:00","id":1392274,"title":"","content":"I am imagining a Troupe Style campaign, where reality and history are quite fluid. Four players. Everyone plays a Mage, a Companion, and two Acolytes. Each player takes a turn running a story. One of them can be the &quot;alpha st&quot; or it can be a committee. A lot of the &quot;surface&quot; reality remains the same from game to game. But each player in turn as a gm can introduce tweaks and alternate takes on chronology. Yet at the same time, anything other than what the characters do in game can be retconned back and forth (and even some of that can be changed). Kind of like living in the DC comics universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T16:19:47-07:00","id":1392347,"title":"","content":"The Lost Paths book says on p. 11 that the Ahl-i-Batin's avatars all come from fragments of 'an ancient spirit called &quot;the Entelechy&quot;', which 'was composed of the highly evolved souls of pre-historical mages that sought to unite and enlighten humanity in the interest of mankind\u2019s well-being. In the last Great Cycle it had been the role of those spirits to guide the dominant species to its destiny'. It also says that when the Entelechy returned to the Tellurian in 514 BCE, this was 'thousands of eons' after its original banishment. So, they seem to be saying reality has gone through multiple 'Great Cycles', the last one probably predates Cain slaying Abel.<br /> <br /> The Entelechy plays a big role in the Ascension scenario, so maybe the ending presented there is just the end of the current Great Cycle? P. 14 of Lost Paths says that when the Entelechy encountered the Tellurian and was shattered, the mages experienced a new Entity called the Khwaja al-Akbar which was 'the Process of the Entelechy\u2019s Passing Away (fana) embodied', and p. 53 of Ascension says '<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Khwaja al-Akbar was more than the massed Avatars of the refugees. It was an emanation from the future \u2014 a future when Ascension had been achieved and <b>the Cycle of Creation</b>, including the Sphere of Telos, was realized'.<br /> <br /> Ascension also has a section starting on p. 52 that talks about some history that presumably is part of the current Cycle but predates ancient Greece, about '</span></span>refugees from the hell-cities of the ancients' who 'fled the infernal despots of Bh\u00e2t, the demonologists of old Babylon and the devil-haunted ruins of places that would be remembered as Gehenna and Babel.' Also talks about how with the help of the Psychopomps, some mages managed to 'sieze power' in these hell-cities, and also ransacked one of the 'infernal temples' to get the Knife of Ixion which Cain had used to slay Abel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26184-jessem","name":"JesseM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T06:15:07-07:00","id":1392490,"title":"","content":"How much of that stuff from <i>Ascension</i> is even canon anymore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T07:40:44-07:00","id":1392522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1322256-what-predates-the-mythic-age-in-mage-s-history?p=1392490#post1392490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much of that stuff from <i>Ascension</i> is even canon anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Ascension</i> was always and explicitly billed as a collection of scenarios and options - some of them mutually contradictory - so I'd have to go with &quot;none of it, away from your table.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;</span>Explanations exist; they have existed for all time; there is always a well-known solution to every human problem \u2014 neat, plausible, and wrong.<span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;<br /> - H.L. Mencken</span></div>","edited":{"userid":467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/467-bob-the-skull","user":"Bob the Skull","date":". 05-29-2020, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/467-bob-the-skull","name":"Bob the Skull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T07:46:29-07:00","id":1392527,"title":"","content":"I would say that the answer is subjective. There are those who are superfans and will not let go of a thing unless a published source instructs them to do so, and even then maybe not. There are those that feel that each individual edition should be taken as a whole and bits previous are to be ignored or are optional at best.<br /> M20 delightfully does all these things!<br /> The various future fates text boxes, they address various bits and pieces of metaplot and cannon, all presented as optional and variable. The base default is that most of the bad stuff from Revised either did not happen, was not as bad as first thought, and/or as gotten better since then.<br /> Every RPG, in theory, has a malleable cannon. M20 is hyper elastic in that regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-29T08:23:42-07:00","id":1392545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marko Markoko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1322256-what-predates-the-mythic-age-in-mage-s-history?p=1392527#post1392527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that the answer is subjective. There are those who are superfans and will not let go of a thing unless a published source instructs them to do so, and even then maybe not. There are those that feel that each individual edition should be taken as a whole and bits previous are to be ignored or are optional at best.<br /> M20 delightfully does all these things!<br /> The various future fates text boxes, they address various bits and pieces of metaplot and cannon, all presented as optional and variable. The base default is that most of the bad stuff from Revised either did not happen, was not as bad as first thought, and/or as gotten better since then.<br /> Every RPG, in theory, has a malleable cannon. M20 is hyper elastic in that regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, M20 has it's issues but how it handles the Metaplot is not one of them.<br /> <br /> It's going to kind of suck if M5 ever happens and we get a definitive Metaplot. Doubly so if they go for the Technocracy as the Alt-Right because that is <u><i><b>PAINFULLY</b></i></u>wrong.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T15:10:48-07:00","id":1392909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1322256-what-predates-the-mythic-age-in-mage-s-history?p=1392490#post1392490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much of that stuff from <i>Ascension</i> is even canon anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, note that in my first paragraph I was just talking about stuff from <i>Lost Paths</i> rather than <i>Ascension</i>, and that's where I saw the info about the Entelechy as a being from the &quot;last Great Cycle&quot; which had been banished from the Tellurian &quot;thousands of eons&quot; before. M20 repeats the basic story of the Entelechy's return being the origin of Ahl-i-Batan souls on p. 202, although it just says the Entelechy was &quot;comprised of the Ascended souls of mages who lived in an age before this one&quot; without specifically saying how ancient it is or anything about a Great Cycle. The notion of a Great Cycle is mentioned on p. 156 in the Euthanatos section but it doesn't elaborate too much on what this means, so it's not clear if they're still talking about very long historical cycles of universal creation and destruction (which the revised Euthanatos tradition book talked about on p. 76-77, using the Hindu idea of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kalpa_(aeon)\" target=\"_blank\">Kalpas</a>) or if they're exclusively talking about the cycles of death and rebirth for individuals.<br /> <br /> Aside from the question of universal cycles, since the OP was asking about anything before the fall of Rome, M20 does include an outline of history on p. 121-123 which goes back a lot further, naming various ages prior to the &quot;High Mythic Ages&quot; after the fall of classical civilizations. And depending on what you want to take as canon, a bunch of the revised Tradition books have information about their history stretching back to before the fall of Rome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26184-jessem","user":"JesseM","date":". 05-30-2020, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26184-jessem","name":"JesseM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T15:40:21-07:00","id":1392924,"title":"","content":"Note that when Exalted first came out, a lot of effort was made to present it as the ancient prehistory of the World of Darkness, and not just in Exalted; the references JesseM cites are among the examples going the other way around. (Likewise, the Imbued from <b>Hunter: the Reckoning</b> were suggested to be the return of the Solar Exalted, albeit severely toned down to prevent them from mutating from solution to problem.) It was mentioned by one of the late-stage Exalted 2e developers that the link between Exalted and World of Darkness wasn't being talked about anymore, but had never been officially rescinded. I don't know if that still holds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T16:55:27-07:00","id":1392942,"title":"","content":"In addition to the Exalted connection, I think some of the stuff about the Great Cycle in the Revised era may have been because they wanted to highlight the idea of some kind of impending apocalypse--I don't know exactly when they made the decision to give the Mage universe a definite wrap-up with the Ascension scenario, but even before that they may have wanted to have more of a sense of the world being on its last legs (p. 263 the Revised core book talks about this aspect of the setting, saying 'Millennial fever has struck the World of Darkness, hard, and it\u2019s tough to ignore the portents that the End Times are near'). This seems especially likely in the section I mentioned on p. 76-77 of the revised Euthanatos book, which talks about the Hindu belief that we're in the Kali Yuga (the last age before the death and rebirth of the universe) and then goes on to say &quot;If the Kali Yuga follows the natural rhythm of the Cycle, it will conclude at the end of the 4300th Century. ... Unfortunately, the Wheel turners suspect that the Age of Kali has fallen from its predetermined course. Nuclear weapons, pollution and turmoil in the Underworld all point to a premature apocalypse \u2014 the destruction of the Wheel rather than its natural rotation.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, the section on p. 12 of Lost Paths where they introduce the Entelechy said it was made up of prehistoric mages whose role in the last Great Cycle was &quot;to guide the dominant species to its destiny&quot;, which sounds like a kind of foreshadowing of Psychopomps and the Telos sphere in Ascension (or may have at least been part of the inspiration for a later decision to make the Entelechy play a big role in the story of their re-emergence).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26184-jessem","name":"JesseM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T17:07:14-07:00","id":1392948,"title":"","content":"\u201cThe end is near\u201d was built into the World of Darkness right from the beginning back in 1991 when Vampire: the Masquerade was first published. The first edition that <i>didn't</i> have an apocalyptic scenario in its immediate future was the 20th Anniversary Editions; and even they tend toward a \u201cteetering on the brink\u201d attitude \u2014 that said, \u201cthe world could end if we screw this up\u201d is a damn sight better than \u201cthe world <i>will</i> end, and soon\u201d of the earlier editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T17:28:06-07:00","id":1392951,"title":"","content":"Sure, in Vampire and Werewolf the &quot;end is near&quot; theme was always very prominent, but the different game lines weren't that closely integrated and I think this was less of a theme in Mage before Revised. In the first and second edition the large-scale drama was mostly focused on the Ascension War between the Traditions and the Technocracy (Nephandi and Marauders were in there too but they seemed like less of a regular threat outside the Umbra), I don't remember any strong hints that the battle was about to come to an end or that something other than those two factions was on the verge of ending it all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26184-jessem","name":"JesseM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T01:29:29-07:00","id":1393036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1322256-what-predates-the-mythic-age-in-mage-s-history?p=1392924#post1392924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that when Exalted first came out, a lot of effort was made to present it as the ancient prehistory of the World of Darkness, and not just in Exalted; the references JesseM cites are among the examples going the other way around. (Likewise, the Imbued from <b>Hunter: the Reckoning</b> were suggested to be the return of the Solar Exalted, albeit severely toned down to prevent them from mutating from solution to problem.) It was mentioned by one of the late-stage Exalted 2e developers that the link between Exalted and World of Darkness wasn't being talked about anymore, but had never been officially rescinded. I don't know if that still holds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's not been even alluded to in 3rd edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T04:51:35-07:00","id":1393057,"title":"","content":"So, not really a change from 2e. (As far as I know, the only hint of it that appeared there was in the \u201cprophecy\u201d in the Sidereal backstory that caused them to arrange for the destruction of the Solars, and which split them into the Gold and Bronze factions: supposedly, the original future that they wanted to prevent was the World of Darkness.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T09:11:24-07:00","id":1393110,"title":"","content":"Right on the back of 2e Core it was very explicit... then it was basically never mentioned again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}